erset of scan-tier\" framing was considered and **rejected** — promoting the deliberately-noisy scan rules to run at capture would silently rewrite innocent text, breaking the near-zero-false-positive invariant. The value-based learning above is the intended narrow form.\n20\t- Store holds plaintext by necessity (fingerprints are one-way, can't drive exact matching); acceptable because `.git/` is as local-and-unshared as the transcripts, per the transport trust boundary.\n21\t\n22\t**Deferred, roughly by urgency:**\n23\t1. Encrypt known-secrets at rest (OS keychain; decrypt must be non-interactive since capture runs silently every turn). `0600` already shipped.\n24\t2. Post-push purge, re-anchor, path-based capture exclusion, auto-renormalize, harness-artifact capture, sub-turn citation anchors.\n25\t\n26\t**Dogfooding note:** this repo captures its own sessions. It once had ~64 benign scan findings (fixtures containing literal `password=supersecret123`-style strings, which no pattern can distinguish from real secrets) that held the ledger push back; as of 2026-07-26 `cledger scan` on this repo reports **no findings** — the allowlist has absorbed them, so the ledger push is no longer blocked. The open question this leaves is the roadmap's \"audit the allowlist for generalizable false-positive patterns\" item: allowlisting is per-repo, so every downstream consumer whose codebase talks *about* secrets hits the same `keyword-assignment` false positives independently.\n27\t\n28\tRelated: [[project-ledger-ecosystem]]\n29\t","tool_use_id":"toolu_01XNrxB3MgzbAFkWRv24nheK","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"worktree-redaction-pre-push-only","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/redaction-pre-push-only","head":"05d08b97689a29e699f8424f739383e853cd8e12","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:a4ea5e90-d87a-4bf6-a351-9d8227a2ef59","seq":434},"id":"ev1-f871