{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_014JzhN4eMqbyDFYHh2MEDHb","input":{"command":"cd /Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/redaction-pre-push-only\ngh pr create --draft --title \"Redaction is pre-push only; reads never prefer the un-redacted copy\" --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\n## What was wrong\n\n`cledger redact` detected the already-pushed case, warned, and **proceeded anyway** — reporting partial success while making the situation strictly worse.\n\nRewriting a shared note line cannot remove it, for structural reasons:\n\n- a notes ref carries **its own commit chain**, so every prior note body travels to every clone and is recoverable with a plain `git log -p refs/notes/conversation-ledger`;\n- `cat_sort_uniq` unions **lines**, so a rewritten line never displaces the original anywhere that still holds it;\n- and `pushScopedNotes` seeds from the remote's tip and unions the local scope into it — so **redact-then-push actively re-uploaded** the pre-redaction line alongside the rewrite, leaving both copies on the remote permanently.\n\nSeparately, reads could surface the plaintext. `dedupById` collapses same-id copies by earliest `recorded_at`, then by a canonical-JSON byte compare. A redacted event and its original share an id *by design* (the rewrite pins it, so a rescan dedups instead of resurrecting the secret) and share `recorded_at` too (the rewrite spreads the original) — so both keys tied and the byte compare decided, resolving on the secret's first character against the `[` (0x5B) opening `[REDACTED:…]`. **Every secret starting with a digit or an uppercase letter sorted below it and won**, so reads printed the plaintext next to the `redaction` event asserting its removal.\n\n## Changes\n\n1. **`redact` refuses post-push**, before mutating anything — and also when `origin` can't be reached to rule it out, since a security decision resting on a failed network call must fail closed (an offline `ls-remote` was previously indistinguishable from a virgin remote). Gating is **per event**, so routine pushing doesn't disable redaction for everything captured afterwards.\n2. **`dedupById` consults redaction depth first** — the copy carrying more `redactions` records wins outright. Unambiguous because capture-time redaction runs *before* ids are computed, leaving `redactEvent` as the only source of same-id/different-content pairs.\n3. **Honest output.** No more `history squashed: yes`. Severing the notes chain is real but is not an object purge; the command now says what remains, that the residue is local-only (git transfers neither reflogs nor unreachable objects), and the one-liner that clears it — rather than running a repo-wide destructive `gc` on the user's behalf.\n4. **Config warns instead of failing open silently** on a malformed-but-present file, which previously reverted every setting to its default — including the opt-in redaction layers whose whole purpose is being switched on.\n\n## Verification\n\nUnit tests plus end-to-end runs against real repos and remotes:\n\n- post-push redaction refuses and leaves the ledger ref **byte-identical** (no half-applied rewrite, no orphan companion event);\n- pre-push redaction still works **after an earlier push**, and the value never appears in a fresh clone's full notes history (`git log -p`);\n- a redacted copy **wins a real `cat_sort_uniq` merge** against a peer still holding the original — the exact case that leaked plaintext before.\n\n`npm test`: 167 pass, 0 fail, 1 skip (pre-existing gitleaks-oracle skip; tool not installed).\n\n## Notes\n\n- Drops `docs/SCRATCH-redaction-does-not-redact.md`, whose subject this resolves (recoverable in history). Its reflog finding was accurate but scoped to local disk; the post-push re-upload path was the severe one and wasn't in it.\n- **Version left at 0.16.0** — PR #2 already claims 0.17.0. Needs a call at merge time.\n- Deferred by design: encrypting the known-secrets store (`redact --pattern` still *adds* a local plaintext copy), and the post-push purge tooling that already-shared content now routes to.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01XKT5PMYyuCnXNyCynZo2ZM\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -3","description":"Open draft PR"},"name":"Bash","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"worktree-redaction-pre-push-only","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/redaction-pre-push-only","head":"05d08b97689a29e699f8424f739383e853cd8e12","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:a4ea5e90-d87a-4bf6-a351-9d8227a2ef59","seq":428},"id":"ev1-9e223233cecc0610f0cc89d1d3400a4dc806a34e5cf29d7ab74cd54d7833a810","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-03T03:28:05.527Z","producer":{"model":"claude-opus-5","session_id":"a4ea5e90-d87a-4bf6-a351-9d8227a2ef59","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.220","tool":"cledger","version":"0.16.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/redaction-pre-push-only","effort":"high","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"worktree-redaction-pre-push-only","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_014JzhN4eMqbyDFYHh2MEDHb","input":{"command":"cd /Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/redaction-pre-push-only\ngh pr create --draft --title \"Redaction is pre-push only; reads never prefer the un-redacted copy\" --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\n## What was wrong\n\n`cledger redact` detected the already-pushed case, warned, and **proceeded anyway** — reporting partial success while making the situation strictly worse.\n\nRewriting a shared note line cannot remove it, for structural reasons:\n\n- a notes ref carries **its own commit chain**, so every prior note body travels to every clone and is