{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"Sanity check before calling it done: full suite is **167 pass, 0 fail, 1 skip** (pre-existing gitleaks-oracle skip, tool not installed), and I re-ran all three real-repo scenarios against the built binary rather than trusting unit tests alone.\n\n**PR #3 (draft):** https://github.com/evintunador/conversation-ledger/pull/3\n\n## What changed\n\n**1. `redact` refuses post-push** — checked before any mutation, so there's no half-applied state. Also refuses when `origin` is unreachable, because an offline `ls-remote` was previously indistinguishable from a virgin remote, and a security decision resting on a failed network call has to fail closed. Gating is **per event**, not per repo — so pushing regularly doesn't kill redaction for everything you capture afterwards. That turned out to matter: the naive \"does origin have the ledger ref\" check would have disabled redaction permanently after your first push.\n\n**2. `dedupById` prefers the redacted copy** — redaction depth outranks both `recorded_at` and the byte compare. Also fixes any repo already sitting in the bad state.\n\n**3. Honest output** — replaced `history squashed: yes` with what actually happened, what remains, and the command that clears it. No destructive gc on your behalf.\n\n**4. Config warns** instead of silently reverting every setting to default.\n\n## Verification that isn't just unit tests\n\n- Post-push redact refuses, ledger ref **byte-identical** afterward — no rewritten line, no orphan companion event.\n- Pre-push redact still works *after* an earlier push, and a fresh clone's full `git log -p` of the notes ref shows the value never left the machine.\n- A redacted copy **wins a real `cat_sort_uniq` merge** against a peer holding the original — the exact case that leaked plaintext before.\n\nOne of those runs initially looked like a regression; it was the new gate correctly refusing a redaction I'd sequenced wrong in the test script, with its stderr swallowed. Worth knowing the gate is aggressive enough to catch that.\n\n## Two things I want to flag\n\n**Version left at 0.16.0.** PR #2 already claims 0.17.0 for the opencode adapter, so bumping here would collide. Needs your call at merge time.\n\n**I deleted `docs/SCRATCH-redaction-does-not-redact.md`** since this resolves its subject (recoverable in history). Its reflog finding was accurate but local-only; the severe path — the scoped push re-uploading the original — wasn't in it. If you'd rather keep it as a record, easy to restore.\n\nStill deferred per your call: encrypting the known-secrets store (so `redact --pattern` still adds a local plaintext copy), and the destructive post-push purge tooling that already-shared content now routes to.\n\nresult: Redaction fixed and scoped to pre-push only — PR #3 (draft) makes `cledger redact` refuse already-pushed or unverifiable events before mutating anything, makes reads always prefer the redacted copy over its pre-redaction original, replaces the false \"history squashed\" claim, and stops config from failing open silently; 167 tests pass plus three real-repo end-to-end verifications.","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"worktree-redaction-pre-push-only","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/redaction-pre-push-only","head":"05d08b97689a29e699f8424f739383e853cd8e12","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:a4ea5e90-d87a-4bf6-a351-9d8227a2ef59","seq":451},"id":"ev1-d4a8fa1df55c24198d73c9fea8a004b19d269711821463eda3ba004c4ef26db8","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-03T03:28:53.749Z","producer":{"model":"claude-opus-5","session_id":"a4ea5e90-d87a-4bf6-a351-9d8227a2ef59","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.220","tool":"cledger","version":"0.16.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/red